00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:35.700
MEMS Strata maintains a bi-temporal ledger that retires stale facts using deterministic subject

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:43.920
relation object supersession rules when contradictions appear. Across six benchmarks with a 7B model,

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:53.540
it matches standard retrieval augmented generation on static knowledge while reaching 0.95 to 1.00 accuracy

00:06:53.540 --> 00:07:01.560
on evolving knowledge where retrieval augmented generation drops to 0.20 to 0.47.

00:07:02.420 --> 00:07:08.580
It eliminates the 15 to 40% stale fact error rate seen in retrieval augmented

00:07:08.580 --> 00:07:17.240
generation at roughly 2.1 seconds retrieval latency. Agent developers handling time sensitive data should

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:24.200
integrate the supersession mechanism to avoid serving outdated information. A developer using open

00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:31.620
router APIs is seeking affordable, controllable open source LLM deployment options that support fine

00:07:31.620 --> 00:07:38.460
tuning without CUDA or Transformers complexity. The post highlights ownership of the full stack

00:07:38.460 --> 00:07:45.580
