00:07:45.580 --> 00:07:52.420
manage platforms or simplified inference servers. Builders facing similar constraints should review

00:07:52.420 --> 00:07:59.440
the thread for current recommendations on private deployment paths. Context forge recycles task relevant

00:07:59.440 --> 00:08:05.960
information across multi-turn conversations using structured query generation, external memory

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:13.080
retrieval and controlled synthesis. On a 15 turn healthcare benchmark, it improves consistency and

00:08:13.080 --> 00:08:18.760
reduces token consumption compared with a baseline agent while maintaining response accuracy.

00:08:19.720 --> 00:08:26.680
Code and evaluation artifacts are available on GitHub. Teams building long horizon agents should

00:08:26.680 --> 00:08:33.560
test the recycling approach to lower context window pressure. Okay, let's pop the hood on delta rule

00:08:33.560 --> 00:08:40.900
memory updates. Everyone talks about delta rule linear attention as a simple correct before you write

00:08:40.900 --> 00:08:47.880
trick. In practice, it still ties the correction to the current right address, so stale value sitting

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:54.520
at other addresses stay untouched until passive decay eventually removes them. The engineering fix

00:08:54.520 --> 00:09:00.720
is to add an independent erase step that first suppresses outdated memory along a learn direction,

00:09:01.320 --> 00:09:07.760
then performs the usual delta correction at the active right location. This adds a second learned

00:09:07.760 --> 00:09:14.360
vector per update but keeps the core delta math intact, preserving the quality of the corrective

00:09:14.360 --> 00:09:22.800
right while giving the model an explicit cleanup path. In 2.5 billion and 25 billion scale pre-training

00:09:22.800 --> 00:09:29.260
runs, the extra path helps most when decay is weak, cutting stale factor tension without

00:09:29.260 --> 00:09:36.740
increasing overall memory bandwidth. The practical takeaway is to adopt the decoupled erase when your

00:09:36.740 --> 00:09:43.840
workload contains frequent value changes. If facts are mostly static, the added vector offers little return

00:09:44.400 --> 00:09:51.880
and the simpler single address delta rule remains preferable. Test Nemotron 2-tower waits on long

00:09:51.880 --> 00:10:00.080
context generation tasks to measure the 2.42 times throughput gain against your current auto-regressive

00:10:00.080 --> 00:10:07.020
baseline. Integrate MEMS stratastyle super-session rules into any retrieval augmented generation

00:10:07.020 --> 00:10:15.500
